{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014SMzdmZGdtqtpCzY5r8NCx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# QuantAgent-82t — Design: Re-enable Unit Tests in CI Pipeline\n2\t\n3\t**Issue ID:** QuantAgent-82t  \n4\t**Title:** Re-enable unit tests in CI pipeline (main-ci-deploy.yml)  \n5\t**Type:** Task\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## Design Overview\n10\t\n11\tUncomment and configure the existing \"Run unit tests\" step in `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml` to restore test execution in the CI pipeline. The PostgreSQL service container is already configured; we only need to activate the test step and ensure it properly blocks deployment on failure.\n12\t\n13\t---\n14\t\n15\t## Affected Components\n16\t\n17\t### Modified\n18\t- `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml` — Uncomment test step (lines 62-69)\n19\t\n20\t### Not Modified\n21\t- `.github/workflows/main-ci.yml` — Different workflow (handled by QuantAgent-ng1)\n22\t- `pytest.ini` — Configuration already correct\n23\t- `tests/` — Test files unchanged\n24\t- PostgreSQL service configuration — Already configured correctly\n25\t\n26\t---\n27\t\n28\t## Technical Changes\n29\t\n30\t### Change 1: Uncomment Test Step\n31\t\n32\t**Current (lines 62-69):**\n33\t```yaml\n34\t# Unit tests temporarily disabled (tracked for later deep dive)\n35\t# - name: Run unit tests\n36\t#   id: tests\n37\t#   env:\n38\t#     DATABASE_URL: postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/quantagent_test\n39\t#   run: |\n40\t#     pytest tests/ -v --tb=short --maxfail=5 \\\n41\t#       -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n42\t#   continue-on-error: true\n43\t```\n44\t\n45\t**After (proposed):**\n46\t```yaml\n47\t- name: Run unit tests\n48\t  id: tests\n49\t  env:\n50\t    DATABASE_URL: postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/quantagent_test\n51\t  run: |\n52\t    pytest tests/ -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 \\\n53\t      -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n54\t```\n55\t\n56\t**Key changes:**\n57\t1. Remove all comment symbols (`#`)\n58\t2. Change `maxfail=5` → `maxfail=10` (see more failures before stopping)\n59\t3. **Remove** `continue-on-error: true` (block deployment on failure)\n60\t\n61\t---\n62\t\n63\t## Design Decisions\n64\t\n65\t### Decision 1: Why Remove `continue-on-error: true`?\n66\t\n67\t**Rationale:**\n68\t- Original intent: Allow CI to continue even if tests fail (during test suite stabilization)\n69\t- **Now:** Tests are fixed (QuantAgent-sfc + QuantAgent-4ch), should enforce quality gate\n70\t- **Benefit:** Prevents broken code from reaching QA\n71\t\n72\t**Alternative considered:** Keep `continue-on-error: true`\n73\t- ❌ **Rejected:** Defeats the purpose of CI tests; broken code still deploys\n74\t\n75\t### Decision 2: Why `maxfail=10` instead of `maxfail=5`?\n76\t\n77\t**Rationale:**\n78\t- More context for debugging when failures occur\n79\t- 10 failures is still fast enough (tests fail-fast)\n80\t- Helps identify patterns in failures vs. single flaky test\n81\t\n82\t**Alternative considered:** Remove `maxfail` entirely (run all tests)\n83\t- ❌ **Rejected:** Wastes CI minutes on known failures; fail-fast is better\n84\t\n85\t### Decision 3: Why Keep Marker Filters `\"not integration and not slow\"`?\n86\t\n87\t**Rationale:**\n88\t- **`not integration`:** Integration tests may require additional setup (external APIs, etc.)\n89\t- **`not slow`:** Keep CI fast (unit tests only)\n90\t- **Matches pytest.ini markers:** Already defined and in use\n91\t\n92\t**Alternative considered:** Run all tests including integration/slow\n93\t- ❌ **Rejected:** CI would be slow; integration tests better suited for nightly/scheduled runs\n94\t\n95\t### Decision 4: PostgreSQL Service Configuration\n96\t\n97\t**Already configured correctly:**\n98\t```yaml\n99\tservices:\n100\t  postgres:\n101\t    image: postgres:16\n102\t    env:\n103\t      POSTGRES_USER: test\n104\t      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: test\n105\t      POSTGRES_DB: quantagent_test\n106\t    ports:\n107\t      - 5432:5432\n108\t    options: >-\n109\t      --health-cmd pg_isready\n110\t      --health-interval 10s\n111\t      --health-timeout 5s\n112\t      --health-retries 5\n113\t```\n114\t\n115\t**No changes needed:**\n116\t- ✅ Correct PostgreSQL version (16)\n117\t- ✅ Test database `quantagent_test` created\n118\t- ✅ Health checks ensure database is ready before tests run\n119\t- ✅ Credentials match `DATABASE_URL` in test step\n120\t\n121\t---\n122\t\n123\t## Workflow Flow After Change\n124\t\n125\t```mermaid\n126\tgraph TD\n127\t    A[Push to main] --> B[Checkout code]\n128\t    B --> C[Setup Python]\n129\t    C --> D[Install dependencies]\n130\t    D --> E[Lint with ruff]\n131\t    E --> F{Lint passed?}\n132\t    F -->|No| G[Notify Telegram - CI Fail]\n133\t    F -->|Yes| H[Run unit tests]\n134\t    H --> I{Tests passed?}\n135\t    I -->|No| J[Notify Telegram - CI Fail]\n136\t    I -->|Yes| K[Notify Telegram - CI Success]\n137\t    K --> L[Deploy to QA]\n138\t    L --> M[Health check]\n139\t    M --> N{Health OK?}\n140\t    N -->|Yes| O[Notify Telegram - Deploy Success]\n141\t    N -->|No| P[Notify Telegram - Deploy Fail]\n142\t```\n143\t\n144\t**Key points:**\n145\t- Tests run **after** lint (existing order preserved)\n146\t- Test failure **blocks** deployment (new behavior)\n147\t- Telegram notifications triggered at each stage\n148\t\n149\t---\n150\t\n151\t## Status Determination Logic\n152\t\n153\t**Existing logic in \"Determine overall status\" step:**\n154\t```yaml\n155\t- name: Determine overall status\n156\t  id: status\n157\t  env:\n158\t    LINT_EXIT: ${{ steps.lint.outcome }}\n159\t    TESTS_EXIT: ${{ steps.tests.outcome || 'skipped' }}\n160\t  run: |\n161\t    if [[ \"$LINT_EXIT\" != \"success\" ]]; then\n162\t      echo \"failed_step=Lint\" >> $GITHUB_OUTPUT\n163\t      exit 1\n164\t    fi\n165\t\n166\t    if [[ \"$TESTS_EXIT\" != \"success\" && \"$TESTS_EXIT\" != \"skipped\" ]]; then\n167\t      echo \"failed_step=Unit tests\" >> $GITHUB_OUTPUT\n168\t      exit 1\n169\t    fi\n170\t\n171\t    echo \"All checks passed\"\n172\t```\n173\t\n174\t**After uncommenting test step:**\n175\t- `TESTS_EXIT` will no longer be `'skipped'`\n176\t- If tests fail, `TESTS_EXIT` will be `'failure'`\n177\t- Status step will fail with `failed_step=Unit tests`\n178\t- Telegram notification will show \"Failed step: Unit tests\"\n179\t\n180\t**No changes needed to this logic** — it already handles test failures correctly.\n181\t\n182\t---\n183\t\n184\t## Alternative Approaches Considered\n185\t\n186\t### ❌ Approach 1: Add `continue-on-error: false` Explicitly\n187\t**Why rejected:**\n188\t- Default behavior is already to fail on error\n189\t- Explicit `false` is redundant\n190\t- Simpler to just remove the line\n191\t\n192\t### ❌ Approach 2: Use Separate Job for Tests\n193\t**Why rejected:**\n194\t- More complex (requires artifact sharing, status checks)\n195\t- Current single-job approach is simpler\n196\t- No benefit for this use case\n197\t\n198\t### ❌ Approach 3: Run Tests Before Lint\n199\t**Why rejected:**\n200\t- Lint is faster; fail fast on style issues first\n201\t- Tests require database setup; slower\n202\t- Existing order is sensible\n203\t\n204\t---\n205\t\n206\t## Testing Strategy\n207\t\n208\t### Pre-Merge Testing\n209\t1. Create test branch with changes\n210\t2. Temporarily push to `main` (or use `workflow_dispatch`)\n211\t3. Verify CI runs tests\n212\t4. Verify test failures block deployment\n213\t5. Verify Telegram notifications sent\n214\t\n215\t### Post-Merge Validation\n216\t1. First commit to `main` after merge should run tests\n217\t2. Monitor GitHub Actions UI\n218\t3. Confirm Telegram notifications received\n219\t4. Verify QA deployment occurs (if tests pass)\n220\t\n221\t---\n222\t\n223\t## Risk Assessment\n224\t\n225\t### Risk 1: Flaky Tests\n226\t**Description:** Intermittent test failures cause false positives\n227\t\n228\t**Mitigation:**\n229\t- QuantAgent-4ch fixed database setup (reduces flakiness)\n230\t- Monitor first few runs closely\n231\t- If flakiness detected, identify and fix root cause\n232\t\n233\t**Probability:** Low (after QuantAgent-4ch fix)  \n234\t**Impact:** Medium (blocked deployments)\n235\t\n236\t### Risk 2: PostgreSQL Service Not Ready\n237\t**Description:** Tests run before PostgreSQL is healthy\n238\t\n239\t**Mitigation:**\n240\t- Service already has health checks configured\n241\t- GitHub Actions waits for healthy status before running tests\n242\t- Tested in existing configuration\n243\t\n244\t**Probability:** Very Low  \n245\t**Impact:** Medium\n246\t\n247\t### Risk 3: Test Suite Too Slow\n248\t**Description:** CI takes too long, slows down development\n249\t\n250\t**Mitigation:**\n251\t- Only run unit tests (exclude `integration` and `slow`)\n252\t- Fail-fast with `maxfail=10`\n253\t- Monitor CI duration; optimize if needed\n254\t\n255\t**Probability:** Low  \n256\t**Impact:** Low\n257\t\n258\t---\n259\t\n260\t## Rollback Plan\n261\t\n262\tIf tests cause issues after re-enabling:\n263\t\n264\t1. **Immediate rollback:**\n265\t   ```bash\n266\t   git revert <commit-hash>\n267\t   git push origin main\n268\t   ```\n269\t\n270\t2. **Re-comment test step** (hotfix):\n271\t   - Add `#` back to lines 62-69\n272\t   - Commit with message: \"Hotfix: Temporarily disable tests (investigate issue)\"\n273\t   - Push to `main`\n274\t\n275\t3. **Investigation:**\n276\t   - Check GitHub Actions logs\n277\t   - Identify root cause\n278\t   - Fix issue in separate branch\n279\t   - Re-enable tests\n280\t\n281\t---\n282\t\n283\t## Success Metrics\n284\t\n285\t### Immediate (Day 1)\n286\t- [ ] Test step runs on first push to `main`\n287\t- [ ] No errors in GitHub Actions logs\n288\t- [ ] Telegram notifications received correctly\n289\t\n290\t### Short-term (Week 1)\n291\t- [ ] 5+ successful CI runs with tests\n292\t- [ ] Zero false positives (flaky tests)\n293\t- [ ] QA deployments only occur when tests pass\n294\t\n295\t### Long-term (Month 1)\n296\t- [ ] Test suite catches at least 1 real bug before QA\n297\t- [ ] CI duration remains < 5 minutes\n298\t- [ ] Developer confidence in CI increases\n299\t\n300\t---\n301\t\n302\t## Open Questions\n303\t\n304\tNone — design is straightforward.\n305\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1343b5b0-b4c1-40c1-9744-443c28dd579a","uuid":"6849ca29-b68a-4b98-9875-201a42a906a5","timestamp":"2026-05-04T17:46:04.759Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/autodev-worktrees/QuantAgent/QuantAgent-82t/implementer-20260504T174542Z/docs/03_design/QuantAgent-82t-DS-ci-test-enablement.md","content":"# QuantAgent-82t — Design: Re-enable Unit Tests in CI Pipeline\n\n**Issue ID:** QuantAgent-82t  \n**Title:** Re-enable unit tests in CI pipeline (main-ci-deploy.yml)  \n**Type:** Task\n\n---\n\n## Design Overview\n\nUncomment and configure the existing \"Run unit tests\" step in `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml` to restore test execution in the CI pipeline. The PostgreSQL service container is already configured; we only need to activate the test step and ensure it properly blocks deployment on failure.\n\n---\n\n## Affected Components\n\n### Modified\n- `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml` — Uncomment test step (lines 62-69)\n\n### Not Modified\n- `.github/workflows/main-ci.yml` — Different workflow (handled by QuantAgent-ng1)\n- `pytest.ini` — Configuration already correct\n- `tests/` — Test files unchanged\n- PostgreSQL service configuration — Already configured correctly\n\n---\n\n## Technical Changes\n\n### Change 1: Uncomment Test Step\n\n**Current (lines 62-69):**\n```yaml\n# Unit tests temporarily disabled (tracked for later deep dive)\n# - name: Run unit tests\n#   id: tests\n#   env:\n#     DATABASE_URL: postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/quantagent_test\n#   run: |\n#     pytest tests/ -v --tb=short --maxfail=5 \\\n#       -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n#   continue-on-error: true\n```\n\n**After (proposed):**\n```yaml\n- name: Run unit tests\n  id: tests\n  env:\n    DATABASE_URL: postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/quantagent_test\n  run: |\n    pytest tests/ -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 \\\n      -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n```\n\n**Key changes:**\n1. Remove all comment symbols (`#`)\n2. Change `maxfail=5` → `maxfail=10` (see more failures before stopping)\n3. **Remove** `continue-on-error: true` (block deployment on failure)\n\n---\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: Why Remove `continue-on-error: true`?\n\n**Rationale:**\n- Original intent: Allow CI to continue even if tests fail (during test suite stabilization)\n- **Now:** Tests are fixed (QuantAgent-sfc + QuantAgent-4ch), should enforce quality gate\n- **Benefit:** Prevents broken code from reaching QA\n\n**Alternative considered:** Keep `continue-on-error: true`\n- ❌ **Rejected:** Defeats the purpose of CI tests; broken code still deploys\n\n### Decision 2: Why `maxfail=10` instead of `maxfail=5`?\n\n**Rationale:**\n- More context for debugging when failures occur\n- 10 failures is still fast enough (tests fail-fast)\n- Helps identify patterns in failures vs. single flaky test\n\n**Alternative considered:** Remove `maxfail` entirely (run all tests)\n- ❌ **Rejected:** Wastes CI minutes on known failures; fail-fast is better\n\n### Decision 3: Why Keep Marker Filters `\"not integration and not slow\"`?\n\n**Rationale:**\n- **`not integration`:** Integration tests may require additional setup (external APIs, etc.)\n- **`not slow`:** Keep CI fast (unit tests only)\n- **Matches pytest.ini markers:** Already defined and in use\n\n**Alternative considered:** Run all tests including integration/slow\n- ❌ **Rejected:** CI would be slow; integration tests better suited for nightly/scheduled runs\n\n### Decision 4: PostgreSQL Service Configuration\n\n**Already configured correctly:**\n```yaml\nservices:\n  postgres:\n    image: postgres:16\n    env:\n      POSTGRES_USER: test\n      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: test\n      POSTGRES_DB: quantagent_test\n    ports:\n      - 5432:5432\n    options: >-\n      --health-cmd pg_isready\n      --health-interval 10s\n      --health-timeout 5s\n      --health-retries 5\n```\n\n**No changes needed:**\n- ✅ Correct PostgreSQL version (16)\n- ✅ Test database `quantagent_test` created\n- ✅ Health checks ensure database is ready before tests run\n- ✅ Credentials match `DATABASE_URL` in test step\n\n---\n\n## Workflow Flow After Change\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[Push to main] --> B[Checkout code]\n    B --> C[Setup Python]\n    C --> D[Install dependencies]\n    D --> E[Lint with ruff]\n    E --> F{Lint passed?}\n    F -->|No| G[Notify Telegram - CI Fail]\n    F -->|Yes| H[Run unit tests]\n    H --> I{Tests passed?}\n    I -->|No| J[Notify Telegram - CI Fail]\n    I -->|Yes| K[Notify Telegram - CI Success]\n    K --> L[Deploy to QA]\n    L --> M[Health check]\n    M --> N{Health OK?}\n    N -->|Yes| O[Notify Telegram - Deploy Success]\n    N -->|No| P[Notify Telegram - Deploy Fail]\n```\n\n**Key points:**\n- Tests run **after** lint (existing order preserved)\n- Test failure **blocks** deployment (new behavior)\n- Telegram notifications triggered at each stage\n\n---\n\n## Status Determination Logic\n\n**Existing logic in \"Determine overall status\" step:**\n```yaml\n- name: Determine overall status\n  id: status\n  env:\n    LINT_EXIT: ${{ steps.lint.outcome }}\n    TESTS_EXIT: ${{ steps.tests.outcome || 'skipped' }}\n  run: |\n    if [[ \"$LINT_EXIT\" != \"success\" ]]; then\n      echo \"failed_step=Lint\" >> $GITHUB_OUTPUT\n      exit 1\n    fi\n\n    if [[ \"$TESTS_EXIT\" != \"success\" && \"$TESTS_EXIT\" != \"skipped\" ]]; then\n      echo \"failed_step=Unit tests\" >> $GITHUB_OUTPUT\n      exit 1\n    fi\n\n    echo \"All checks passed\"\n```\n\n**After uncommenting test step:**\n- `TESTS_EXIT` will no longer be `'skipped'`\n- If tests fail, `TESTS_EXIT` will be `'failure'`\n- Status step will fail with `failed_step=Unit tests`\n- Telegram notification will show \"Failed step: Unit tests\"\n\n**No changes needed to this logic** — it already handles test failures correctly.\n\n---\n\n## Alternative Approaches Considered\n\n### ❌ Approach 1: Add `continue-on-error: false` Explicitly\n**Why rejected:**\n- Default behavior is already to fail on error\n- Explicit `false` is redundant\n- Simpler to just remove the line\n\n### ❌ Approach 2: Use Separate Job for Tests\n**Why rejected:**\n- More complex (requires artifact sharing, status checks)\n- Current single-job approach is simpler\n- No benefit for this use case\n\n### ❌ Approach 3: Run Tests Before Lint\n**Why rejected:**\n- Lint is faster; fail fast on style issues first\n- Tests require database setup; slower\n- Existing order is sensible\n\n---\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Pre-Merge Testing\n1. Create test branch with changes\n2. Temporarily push to `main` (or use `workflow_dispatch`)\n3. Verify CI runs tests\n4. Verify test failures block deployment\n5. Verify Telegram notifications sent\n\n### Post-Merge Validation\n1. First commit to `main` after merge should run tests\n2. Monitor GitHub Actions UI\n3. Confirm Telegram notifications received\n4. Verify QA deployment occurs (if tests pass)\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n### Risk 1: Flaky Tests\n**Description:** Intermittent test failures cause false positives\n\n**Mitigation:**\n- QuantAgent-4ch fixed database setup (reduces flakiness)\n- Monitor first few runs closely\n- If flakiness detected, identify and fix root cause\n\n**Probability:** Low (after QuantAgent-4ch fix)  \n**Impact:** Medium (blocked deployments)\n\n### Risk 2: PostgreSQL Service Not Ready\n**Description:** Tests run before PostgreSQL is healthy\n\n**Mitigation:**\n- Service already has health checks configured\n- GitHub Actions waits for healthy status before running tests\n- Tested in existing configuration\n\n**Probability:** Very Low  \n**Impact:** Medium\n\n### Risk 3: Test Suite Too Slow\n**Description:** CI takes too long, slows down development\n\n**Mitigation:**\n- Only run unit tests (exclude `integration` and `slow`)\n- Fail-fast with `maxfail=10`\n- Monitor CI duration; optimize if needed\n\n**Probability:** Low  \n**Impact:** Low\n\n---\n\n## Rollback Plan\n\nIf tests cause issues after re-enabling:\n\n1. **Immediate rollback:**\n   ```bash\n   git revert <commit-hash>\n   git push origin main\n   ```\n\n2. **Re-comment test step** (hotfix):\n   - Add `#` back to lines 62-69\n   - Commit with message: \"Hotfix: Temporarily disable tests (investigate issue)\"\n   - Push to `main`\n\n3. **Investigation:**\n   - Check GitHub Actions logs\n   - Identify root cause\n   - Fix issue in separate branch\n   - Re-enable tests\n\n---\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n### Immediate (Day 1)\n- [ ] Test step runs on first push to `main`\n- [ ] No errors in GitHub Actions logs\n- [ ] Telegram notifications received correctly\n\n### Short-term (Week 1)\n- [ ] 5+ successful CI runs with tests\n- [ ] Zero false positives (flaky tests)\n- [ ] QA deployments only occur when tests pass\n\n### Long-term (Month 1)\n- [ ] Test suite catches at least 1 real bug before QA\n- [ ] CI duration remains < 5 minutes\n- [ ] Developer confidence in CI increases\n\n---\n\n## Open Questions\n\nNone — design is straightforward.\n","numLines":305,"startLine":1,"totalLines":305}}}
